# "Search your library for a Swamp or Forest card" is a search by land type (CR 205.3i): the first Catacombs finds Bayou (a Swamp
# Forest), a card that is neither basic, while an Island and a Plains are refused. The second, on turn 3, is answered with nothing (a
# quality search may find nothing, CR 701.23b): it is still sacrificed and the life still paid. (The existing scenario finds a Forest.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Verdant Catacombs
Verdant Catacombs
Island x5
Bayou
Plains
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Verdant Catacombs.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Verdant Catacombs.Activate
! Bot1.Search(Island)
! Bot1.Search(Plains)
Bot1.Search(Bayou)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Verdant Catacombs.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Verdant Catacombs.Activate
Bot1.Search()

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot1.Graveyard = Verdant Catacombs; Verdant Catacombs
Bot1.Battlefield = Bayou
